{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>If</b> — those slain were the cause of others inquiring, or the meaning is 'then He said to slay them,' or 'nearly and He slew them.'" "<b>And they returned</b> — they repented." "<b>And they sought El</b> — that prayer is in the morning, before a person occupies himself with matters of his needs."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 78, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:35:08.505909497Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}